WEBVTT

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.070
System... all green...

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.670
Initiating 300-second countdown until 
network jammer activated...

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.840
Now...

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.450
But, I'm sorry...

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.330
We've lost both the time, and the words...

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.620
to explain everything...

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.790
Please forgive me, Finé...

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.380
Magnetic flux density around the Pole of 
Inaccessibility is transitioning fractally!

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.590
Raising threat level from 3 to 4!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.420
It's advanced far beyond what 
our calculated predictions!

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.050
It appears to match the Wielders' 
arrival almost exactly.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.030
Putting together the information 
and observation data,

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.490
the coffin is most likely a relic 
of a precursor civilization.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.330
Energy signals beneath subglacial lake 
Vostok are exponentially increasing!

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.330
The numbers won't stop going up!

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.570
Here it comes, huh?

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.030
Everyone, prepare for the coffin to surface!

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.760
It's so cold! I'm going numb!

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.250
Who was it that said that it was summer
 in the Southern Hemisphere?

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.290
Yeah!

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:02.420
It's the South Pole. It's cold even in summer.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.260
Once you put your gear on, 
the anti-heat field will—

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.020
That's pretty... bone-chilling.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.430
That's... the coffin?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.080
Kiri-chan, what's a coffin again?

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.790
Don't ask me something a 
normal person shouldn't know!

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.460
The unexpected is always expected! Let's go!

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:55.270
<i>Balwisyall nescell Gungnir tron.</i>

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:40.670
<i>If you've crossed over many darknesses</i>

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:45.410
<i>You can see the dawn sky the light points to</i>

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.020
It's as strong as we are?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.400
But even so...

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.990
<i>So many emotions carved into my heart</i>

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.010
Our feelings are stronger!

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:57.370
<i>The memoria burned into it 
are more than just pain!</i>

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.970
What the hell are those things?

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.070
<i>For what? For who?</i>

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:58.630
What do we do?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.250
The only thing we can do. Stop them!

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.910
<i>What do my instincts say?</i>

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.750
<i>Get to Heart! Get to Heart!</i>

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.210
Split up and get close!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.630
<i>Let my strike burn!</i>

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.630
Don't let it near the observation post!

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.110
<i>Can you hear me (Burnin'!)</i>

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:15.300
<i>Heart (Burnin'!) Soul (Burnin'!) This song!</i>

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.230
<b>α Style 100 Samsara</b>

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.930
<i>No weight will dwell in 
a fist without hesitation</i>

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.090
<b>Kill Juliet</b>

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:25.830
<i>Just hold the answer that 
connects in your hands</i>

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.500
<i>The journey continues 
to know its true meaning</i>

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.840
<i>The wind pushes me forward!</i>

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.450
It didn't work?!

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.010
It's ruthlessly trying to eliminate 
anything that gets close to it.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:51.970
<i>I swear to protect someone, but...</i>

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.330
Can we really call it a coffin?

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.440
This is defense, not offense.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:57.380
<i>I just have two hands, what if 
they're not good enough someday?</i>

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.750
If this is some kind of function
 to ward off grave robbers,

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.650
then it's definitely a coffin.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.650
<i>Even when I'm afraid, I can't stop</i>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.200
<i>Which means what rests in 
the coffin may truly be...</i>

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:08.440
<i>Time continues cruelly towards the future!</i>

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.960
Commander, the coffin's doing something new!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.540
<i>When I make that decision, am I truly me?</i>

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.320
<i>Please tell me! Please tell me!</i>

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:22.630
<i>But just for now, take a step forward!</i>

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:26.790
<i>Let today be the spark that ignites tomorrow</i>

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:31.520
<i>Live so you won't regret your choices</i>

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.640
They're trying to pin us down!

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:35.020
<i>Live now! Live now! You're not done yet!</i>

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.690
It won't work, yeah!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.570
<i>Something still burns within you</i>

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:43.110
<i>Let the fear of the power and its 
possibilities burn bright in your heart</i>

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.910
Don't worry too much about 
this flock of swallows!

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.830
I'll open a path, then!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.910
<i>And believe in the flame!</i>

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:49.940
The way is open!

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.420
The shortest route, as fast as possible!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.910
Straight ahead! In a straight line!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.470
It's working! That's all!

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.910
Guys!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.460
Are you okay?

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:34.820
It's coming!

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.280
Make it in time!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.030
Confirmed damage reduction 
from the Reflector!

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.310
Analysis of the coffin's attack complete!

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.620
Directed energy waves at minus 5100 degrees.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.600
What the hell is this?

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:05.940
Interference with the laws of the 
universe via outer physics...

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:11.740
The fields our gears currently project
 can't block too many of those attacks!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:21.590
<i>Look up at the sun,</i>

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:26.380
<i>Learn about many types of love,</i>

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:31.170
<i>voices loud in the morning and evening,</i>

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:36.540
<i>live strong with the melody</i>

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:40.810
<i>Even if you cry</i>

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.230
<b>Music
Room</b>

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.730
<i>At the end of a distant future</i>

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:50.340
<i>Be proud with your chest held high, maiden</i>

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:58.940
<i>Turning your dreams you believe in into song</i>

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.590
Okay, you pass.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.670
Really? Yes!

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.460
I'm so glad.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.080
Tachibana-san! Don't celebrate yet!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:25.380
I said you pass, but there are still 
many skills you need to learn!

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:29.080
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.490
However...

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.850
Your song was beautiful.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:38.320
I'm sure it's because you're 
singing in your heart.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.180
My heart? The song in my heart!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.240
Sensei!

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.540
Okay, your after-school 
test is now completed.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.660
I know you're busy, 
but don't skip the next test!

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:58.760
I'm glad you found a good birthday present.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.120
Do you think Chris-chan will be happy?

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.960
I'm sure she will.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.860
<i>Now, an update on the exciting 
moon development project.</i>

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:13.730
<i>The long-running US-Japan Joint 
Space Development Project,</i>

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.980
<b>US-Japan Joint Space Development Project Advances</b>

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.990
<b>US-Japan Joint Space Development Project Advances</b>

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:18.200
<i>has announced great progress after 
high-level negotiations between both countries.</i>

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.490
<i>In a sign of thawing relations,</i>

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.870
<b>US-Japan Joint Space Development Project Advances</b>

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.880
<i>they will soon take the first step
 toward reaching the moon,</i>

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.570
<i>a historic agreement for both countries.</i>

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.950
The moon?

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.700
You're so slow! What's wrong?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.750
Sorry, sorry!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.820
I'm kind of hungry.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.220
What? You're paying, Hibiki.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.400
Fine, I guess.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:50.630
The song in my heart's saved me so 
many times, I've lost count, you know?

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.110
Yeah, really!

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:56.390
Lately, my life's been so 
normal, it feels special.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:59.460
It makes me realize how important normal is.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:02.110
You've been going on mission
after mission for a while now.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:06.700
Whenever somebody needs you, 
you race out the door.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.040
If I were in trouble,
 would you come to save me?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:16.300
Of course! I'd be there in a flash for you!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.630
So what if I was causing trouble for someone?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.160
Just hypothetically!

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.780
That's a mean question!

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:32.010
You're taking it too seriously!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.910
Hibiki...

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:38.660
Yeah!

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.570
Hibiki-san, get in!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.150
Miku-san, you, too!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:03.790
There was an accident at a S.O.N.G. research 
facility disguised as a cruise ship.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.600
A floating lab?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:11.390
Was it researching something too 
dangerous to handle in the city?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.490
Yes.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:17.390
We were investigating the remains 
of the Autoscorer we recovered.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.620
We were attempting to examine 
the destroyed Antikythera Gear

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.270
and the Autoscorer's remains 
to discover the goals

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:30.350
of the Bavarian Illuminati 
and Adam Weishaupt.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.200
The explosion that we saw 
may have been triggered

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:37.960
by the safeties protecting
 their deepest secrets...

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:43.180
That Autoscorer they called Tiki 
appeared to have the ability to observe

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.080
the movements of the stars,

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:48.110
and use that recorded data to 
calculate various phenomenon.

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.060
Is that... Antarctica?

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:59.360
The data we recovered before the explosion
 indicated this point at the South Pole.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:04.250
It's Lake Vostok. One of the 
largest lakes in Antarctica.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:07.650
There's a Russian observation post near it.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:12.370
Where's the lake? All I see is snow.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.770
Most of that snow is Lake Vostok.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:19.210
It's under the ice, actually.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:24.730
Earth's environment isn't static. 
It's undergone many changes.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:28.240
These changes have been 
especially stark in recent years,

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.100
and much of the polar ice has been lost.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.630
You're not going to tell me that 
something came out of the ice, are you?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.380
That's just it.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:44.050
This frozen scorpion was found near the 
Vostok observation post the other day.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.440
Investigations revealed it to be a species

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:50.080
that lived in the Middle East 
several thousand years ago.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:53.200
We're told it's presently extinct.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.840
What's something like that 
doing at the South Pole?

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.180
We're currently investigating.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.590
But if you take it at face value,

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:06.330
it implies a precursor civilization brought 
it there from the Middle East, somehow.

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:10.690
That's not the only thing that's concerning.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:17.550
Our agents are hunting down the survivors of 
the Bavarian Illuminati who went underground,

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.940
and continuing their investigation.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:23.470
The information they found indicates 
that Adam was attempting

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:27.910
to use the power of the gods 
to accomplish some goal.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.520
What goal is that?

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:34.120
In order to rule the planet,

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.340
he would destroy the coffin that surfaces 
from beyond the horizon of time.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:38.820
What?

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:42.070
That "surfaces from beyond 
the horizon of time"

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:45.550
seems to match eerily with that scorpion
 they found at the South Pole.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:50.530
Our next mission is an 
investigation at the South Pole.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:53.530
With the Illuminati's survivors 
as our information source,

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:56.570
it's possible the whole thing's a trap.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:01.520
The operation will begin in one week. 
Everyone, get ready!

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:03.100
Roger!

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:15.370
Hope was destroyed today.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.230
Despair of tomorrow, of the future!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.730
Hmm...

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.660
They got taken down easily, huh?

00:14:56.380 --> 00:15:00.350
Even if they're fighting something gigantic 
we wouldn't stand a chance against,

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.200
I'd hope they'd put in more effort.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.590
So? Is it going well?

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.380
We just saw the coffin surface.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:16.380
Did the director really 
try to stop that thing?

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:22.020
To stop the coffin from reviving, 
so he could rule the planet?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.770
There's no way of knowing at this point.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:29.350
If nothing else, our goal and his differ.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:38.880
We're not trying to destroy the coffin.

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.930
We want to put it to good use.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:45.820
Yes... This is a battle 
to take back our future,

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.360
so we have to succeed!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.010
The six Wielders are still unconscious!

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.100
At this rate...

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:58.050
Commander!

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.470
Don't worry. I wore extra-warm underpants.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:03.350
I'll finish things before I freeze.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.690
That's not it...

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.310
A star shell!

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.970
The coffin has stopped moving forward!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.580
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.580
<i>Those girls are out there 
in the freezing cold!</i>

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.750
<i>If they catch cold it'll be really bad!</i>

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:26.850
I knew this would happen!

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.580
Everyone is here!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.420
Everyone!

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:45.010
You want to be a hero that badly?

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:48.980
That's right! You're not the 
only one on the battlefield!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:54.140
Everyone, I'll do my best with my own battle!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.390
<i>So...</i>

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:58.620
Everyone's pushing me forward!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:10.800
<i>I always kept taking one step forward</i>

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:15.160
<i>Without time to wipe my tears away</i>

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:21.300
<i>And those tears soaked deep into my songs</i>

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:25.740
<i>I cried again when I couldn't fly!</i>

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:32.140
<i>My hand grasps for the warm sun, 
but it doesn't reach!</i>

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:35.410
<i>And it's so painful</i>

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.750
<i>I struggled and fought,</i>

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:44.930
<i>but the sky I looked up at was so distant 
and high that I sobbed powerlessly</i>

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:54.670
<i>Swords of words I spat to keep 
away understanding hurt me instead</i>

00:17:54.920 --> 00:18:04.430
<i>But the past I believed in, the past that 
I shed, is the bonds I wove with everyone!</i>

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.470
Are you okay?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:09.690
<i>Now's the time to turn the paths 
you brought together into power!</i>

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.680
Over here, too?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.820
Incoming barrage!

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.140
Punch it!

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:11.990
I don't understand a word you're saying!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:13.330
<i>There's a song I sing for tomorrow</i>

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:16.080
<i>The world is filled with song</i>

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:19.060
<i>Blow, wind of Axia!</i>

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.060
Adjusting the defense field on her fist!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.760
<i>Carrying our tears</i>

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.820
It was a rush job, but Elfnein-chan 
made sure we made it in time!

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.100
<i>You're not alone, connect!</i>

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.630
<i>Even if you flinch, look forward!</i>

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:28.860
Analyzing and reconstructing is the 
fundamental principal of alchemy!

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.420
<i>Stand up even if you're scared</i>

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:30.830
<i>The history mankind has created</i>

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:30.830
This is my battle!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.680
<i>We won't fall even if we die!</i>

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.210
<i>One for all!</i>

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.280
<i>Flowers of the future</i>

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.640
<i>All for one!</i>

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.600
<i>To make them bloom!</i>

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:40.990
<i>Live your life to the fullest!</i>

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:50.070
Hurry to S.O.N.G.'s designated 
evacuation point!

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:51.680
Th-Thank you!

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:53.490
Hurry!

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.800
I won't let you!

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.780
It broke through the ice?!

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.940
Seems so, yes!

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.390
That idiot!

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:31.680
She can't sing underwater, 
so it'll reduce her gear's power!

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:37.920
<i>But even so...</i>

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:42.220
<i>there's a song in my heart!</i>

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:07.850
Are you okay, Tachibana?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.500
Forget me. We need to 
do something about that!

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.840
We should aim for the damaged 
point on its throat!

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:16.410
Concentrate all the energy 
of your gears on one point!

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:20.160
Use our finishers on a moving 
target? If we miss...

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.870
We'd be doomed! We can't!

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.080
Aiming is a sniper's job.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.830
I'll tell you when.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.000
Let's go, everyone!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.700
Right!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.570
Gear Blast!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.450
We can calculate the path, too!

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.720
Wait! There's something around the coffin!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.760
They're acting as reflectors?

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.860
<i>Distance 1,500...</i>

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:45.730
<i>1,200!</i>

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:48.120
Chris-chan, it's almost your birthday!

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.800
When this fight is over...

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:52.990
Jinx yourself, not me!

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.510
Is it time? Is it time?

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:58.490
We're gonna get squished!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.530
<i>Stay calm. Stay calm.</i>

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.670
<i>Make them stay calm.</i>

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:06.680
Now!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:12.320
G3FA! Hexa-Revolver!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:30.930
<b>From the Horizon of Mankind's History</b>

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:27.920
So that's a Custodian...

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:31.270
The body of an Anunnaki, 
the ones they called gods...

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.630
What they call a holy corpse.
